<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 19 November, from 461 to 1977.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">461 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,565 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Libius Severus is proclaimed Western Roman emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Libius Severus, a native of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucania">Lucania</a>, became Western Roman emperor after the general Ricimer overthrew his predecessor Majorian. He was the first of a series of emperors highly dependent on Ricimer, who is often presumed to have held most real power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1493">1493 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">533 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Columbus lands on Puerto Rico</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On his second voyage, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a> landed on the island the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taino">Taíno</a> called Borikén and named it San Juan Bautista. The name of its port, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, later passed to the whole island.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/spanish-empire">Spanish Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Christopher Columbus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1794">1794 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Jay Treaty is signed in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Jay and Lord Grenville signed a treaty settling disputes left over from the Revolutionary War, including British forts in the north-west. Unpopular in America, it nonetheless averted war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1808">1808 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">218 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Convention of Olkijoki ends the fighting in Finland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">With Russian forces having overrun all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a>, the Convention of Olkijoki, signed at Raahe, ended hostilities there and forced the Swedish army to leave the Finnish countryside. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> ceded Finland to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-fredrikshamn">Treaty of Fredrikshamn</a> in 1809.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-war">Finnish War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1863">1863 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">163 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lincoln delivers the Gettysburg Address</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the dedication of the Soldiers' National Cemetery, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abraham-lincoln">Abraham Lincoln</a> spoke for about two minutes. His short address recast the Civil War as a struggle for 'a new birth of freedom' and government 'of the people'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1885">1885 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">141 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bulgaria defeats Serbia at the Battle of Slivnitsa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The battle near Slivnitsa, west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sofia">Sofia</a>, which began on 17 November, ended with the Bulgarian army under Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-of-battenberg">Alexander of Battenberg</a> defeating the invading Serbian army of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> I. The victory secured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>'s union with Eastern Rumelia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-slivnitsa">Battle of Slivnitsa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbo-bulgarian-war">Serbo-Bulgarian War</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1942">1942 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">84 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Red Army launches Operation Uranus at Stalingrad</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet forces attacked the weak Romanian-held flanks north and south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Stalingrad</a>. Within four days they encircled the German Sixth Army, which surrendered in February 1943.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1977">1977 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">49 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Anwar Sadat becomes the first Arab leader to visit Israel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> flew to Israel and the next day addressed the Knesset in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. His visit led to the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords and the 1979 Egyptian-Israeli peace treaty.</p></div></li></ol>
